- qjs-swallows-uncaught-exceptions-with-native-module: NOT a qjs-opencv
  bug - root cause lives in the `qjs` CLI / QuickJS engine itself (a
  separate project, not this repo), recorded here only because it was
  discovered while chasing an unrelated-looking "process exits silently"
  symptom. Confirmed the opencv module is not implicated:
  `import * as std from 'std'; gc();` (no opencv involved at all)
  reproduces the same silent exit(0) with no error printed, whereas the
  identical script with no import correctly prints the exception and
  exits 1. So this is a bug in how `qjs` reports uncaught top-level
  exceptions once *any* native module has been dynamically loaded via the
  module system - out of scope to fix from qjs-opencv. Worth reporting
  upstream / fixing in the quickjs project directly if it matters (it
  currently means any qjs-opencv script's uncaught errors are invisible).

    import * as std from 'std';
    console.log("before");
    gc(); // or any other uncaught exception
    console.log("after"); // never reached, and no error is printed either;
                           // process exits 0. Without the import, the
                           // same script prints the ReferenceError and
                           // exits 1 as expected.

- opencv-tokenizer-load-config-json-format-undocumented: `cv::dnn::Tokenizer::
  load(modelDir)` (OpenCV 5.0+) throws `Assertion failed: buf in function
  'open'` from `opencv2/core/persistence.cpp` when given a real
  `tokenizer.json` (verified with Qwen2.5's actual byte-level-BPE
  tokenizer.json from HuggingFace, see tests/qwen2.5-tokenizer/) alongside a
  `config.json` containing `{"model_type": "gpt2"}` - the exact format the
  Tokenizer::load() doc comment in dnn.hpp describes. Tried several config.json
  variants (compact/pretty JSON, a %YAML:1.0 marker) with identical results,
  so the format cv::FileStorage actually expects here is not what the header
  documents, or the fixture's tokenizer.json itself isn't in the exact dialect
  expected. Not a qjs-opencv binding bug - the exception is a normal
  `cv::Exception`, caught cleanly, no crash - but it means real Qwen2.5
  tokenization is not yet verified end-to-end through this binding. See
  migration-opencv5.md, "Wrapping LLM inference (Qwen2.5)".

    import { dnn } from 'opencv';
    // tests/qwen2.5-tokenizer/{tokenizer.json,config.json} as shipped
    dnn.Tokenizer.load('tests/qwen2.5-tokenizer/'); // throws the above

